      "message": "Lokesh asked me why 4K CoW on anon-THP made 2M dirty, instead of 4K.\n\nThe reason is old-THP couldn\u0027t handle two different granularity(e.g., 4K in child and 2M in parent) mappings in a shared huge page due to page reference counting problem. Since then, it had improved to deal with such mappings so we don\u0027t need to make 2M dirty any longer. The file-THP already has worked like that but we had missed in anon-THP and fixed it in 5.8-rc1, finally.\n\nI am not sure I need to submit this patch into ACK because we don\u0027t decide to enable THP yet(correct?).\nFurthermore, I am not sure it\u0027s a good idea to submit a patch into common tree for personal ongoing project without the formal decision.\n\nThis patch doesn\u0027t have a bug number. Lokesh, please file a bug with justification so others could estimate maintenance risk vs. benefit. The reason I am uploading this patch without specific reason from my mind is this is *generally* good thing(iow, there is no reason to make 2M dirty even though we just touched the 4K page).",
